    "bio": "Indu Antony is a multidisciplinary artist based in Bengaluru and Kerala whose practice spans visual arts, public interventions, olfactory art, publishing, community engagement, and feminist discourse. Her work explores themes of gender, memory, identity, public space, and belonging, often using unconventional artistic mediums to spark social conversations. \n\nShe is also widely known for Vāsané (meaning \"smell\" in Kannada), an award-winning artistic and research project that archives Bengaluru through its scents. Rather than documenting the city visually, Indu collected oral histories from hundreds of residents and identified over 137 smells associated with Bengaluru, eventually distilling them into a sensory archive and book. The project captures everything from filter coffee and Iyengar bakery sponge cake to flower markets, Mysore Sandal Soap, rain-soaked streets, and even polluted lakes—preserving the city's emotional and cultural memory through smell. ",
